    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is fully wired: `OwnerDto` now has `riskFlag`, and the generated `OwnerMapperImpl` calls `riskFlag(owner)`. Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model so it returns `true` when any of the three risk conditions hold, `false` otherwise.\n\n**Design** \u2014 `riskFlag` is a derived read-only field, computed purely from the owner entity in `OwnerMapper` (the same pattern as `ownerSegment`, `membershipLevel`, `possibleDuplicate`, etc.). I mapped each spec condition onto the codebase's existing concepts:\n\n| Spec condition | Implementation |\n|---|---|\n| owner is a possible duplicate | the stored `possibleDuplicate` flag |\n| city is over its soft capacity | the stored `capacityWarning` flag (city already held 40+ owners \u2014 past the soft cap of 40, below the hard cap of 50 that rejects the create) |\n| email domain is disposable-adjacent | new `disposableAdjacent(email)` check |\n\n**\"Disposable-adjacent\"** needed a fresh definition: the controller's existing `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` are *rejected* at create, so a stored owner can never carry one \u2014 a flag keyed to that blocklist could never fire. So I defined it as a *near-miss* to the blocklist: a domain that isn't itself blocked but carries a known disposable provider's second-level label (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) as one of its dot-separated labels \u2014 catching subdomains (`mail.mailinator.com`) and other-TLD variants (`mailinator.net`). A normal or absent email yields `false`.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` readOnly boolean to the Owner schema (generates `OwnerDto`), with a description of all three triggers.\n- `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `@Mapping` for `riskFlag`, the `riskFlag(owner)` derivation, the `disposableAdjacent(email)` helper, and the `DISPOSABLE_PROVIDER_LABELS` set.\n\nThe existing/new acceptance test `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` (a fully unique owner \u2192 `riskFlag == false`) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
